{"name":"Fleur de Sel","hex":"#dcddd8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fleur de sel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Floating salt crystals skimmed from the surface of evaporation ponds, used in cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fleur_de_sel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fleur de Sel","blocks":[{"text":"Fleur de Sel was a restaurant in the Flatiron District of Manhattan in New York City. It had received a Michelin star."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fleur_de_Sel","wikidata":"Q122166640"},{"title":"Fleur de sel","blocks":[{"text":"Fleur de sel or flor de sal is a salt that forms as a thin, delicate crust on the surface of seawater as it evaporates. Fleur de sel has been collected since ancient times, and was traditionally used as a purgative and salve. It is now used as a finishing salt to flavor and garnish food. The origin of the name is uncertain, but is perfectly in line with both meanings of fleur: flower, and the surface of something. The salt crust forms flower-like patterns of crystals which may contribute to the name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/FleurDeSel.JPG/330px-FleurDeSel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fleur_de_sel","wikidata":"Q2167413"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Hamla_Mourad_11.jpg/500px-Hamla_Mourad_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Hamla_Mourad_11.jpg/1280px-Hamla_Mourad_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Hamla_Mourad_11.jpg/500px-Hamla_Mourad_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Formation of fleur de sel in Feraoun (Algeria)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHamla_Mourad_11.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Fleur_de_Sel_de_Gu%C3%A9rande_2026.jpg/500px-Fleur_de_Sel_de_Gu%C3%A9rande_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Fleur_de_Sel_de_Gu%C3%A9rande_2026.jpg/1280px-Fleur_de_Sel_de_Gu%C3%A9rande_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Fleur_de_Sel_de_Gu%C3%A9rande_2026.jpg/500px-Fleur_de_Sel_de_Gu%C3%A9rande_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Packaged Fleur de Sel de Guérande (hand-harvested sea salt) offered for sale at the Marché Bastille open-air market in Paris, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFleur_de_Sel_de_Gu%C3%A9rande_2026.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Gu%C3%A9rande_-_Comparaison_en_Fleur_de_sel_et_Gros_sel.JPG/500px-Gu%C3%A9rande_-_Comparaison_en_Fleur_de_sel_et_Gros_sel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Gu%C3%A9rande_-_Comparaison_en_Fleur_de_sel_et_Gros_sel.JPG/1280px-Gu%C3%A9rande_-_Comparaison_en_Fleur_de_sel_et_Gros_sel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Gu%C3%A9rande_-_Comparaison_en_Fleur_de_sel_et_Gros_sel.JPG/500px-Gu%C3%A9rande_-_Comparaison_en_Fleur_de_sel_et_Gros_sel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Difference between fleur de sel (left) and coarse salt (right) from the salterns of Guérande","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGu%C3%A9rande_-_Comparaison_en_Fleur_de_sel_et_Gros_sel.JPG"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","im